message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "SciMetricsPro: a browser-based platform for bibliometric and scientometric analysis"
abstract: >-
  SciMetricsPro is a self-contained web application for bibliometric and scientometric analysis
  that runs entirely in the browser, with no installation and no server-side computation. It takes
  a set of bibliographic records from the search to the paper: it helps write the search string for
  each academic database, reads their exports (CSV, RIS, BibTeX, tagged text and spreadsheets) and
  downloads records from an open bibliographic catalogue, merges duplicates and normalises authors,
  institutions and countries, computes the classical indicators (annual growth, document age,
  Bradford's law, Lotka's law with a Kolmogorov-Smirnov test, h, g and m indices, local citations
  and reference publication year spectroscopy), and maps the conceptual, intellectual and social
  structures (keyword co-occurrence, thematic map and thematic evolution, correspondence analysis
  with k-means, co-citation, bibliographic coupling, coupling map, direct-citation historiograph,
  collaboration networks and a world collaboration map). It also records a PRISMA 2020 systematic
  review with its flow diagram, and exports journal-ready figures, tables, network files, the clean
  data set and an automatic report with a methods section written from the data.
